WEBVTT

00:01.620 --> 00:03.890
<i>The day after our field lesson,</i>

00:03.890 --> 00:09.360
<i>the principal gave me a warning for 
using the Monster-Calling Flute.</i>

00:09.570 --> 00:14.010
Really? I didn't know the dark 
attribute also had healing magic.

00:14.790 --> 00:18.370
Yes. It can regrow an arm, at least.

00:18.880 --> 00:22.630
Regrow an arm? Are you... 
speaking from experience?

00:23.690 --> 00:24.130
Yes.

00:25.170 --> 00:28.990
When I was a child, my arm 
was sliced off, right here.

00:28.990 --> 00:30.260
Ah...

00:30.620 --> 00:33.230
<i>That sure was a close call.</i>

00:33.230 --> 00:34.980
<i>If that slice had been off by just a hair,</i>

00:34.980 --> 00:37.990
<i>it might've been my head that got severed.</i>

00:37.990 --> 00:41.510
<i>And no healing magic can regrow a head...</i>

00:43.480 --> 00:44.870
<i>Can it?</i>

00:45.910 --> 00:48.810
Anyway, enough of my childhood stories.

00:49.400 --> 00:51.910
How did the central nobles' lesson go?

00:52.870 --> 00:57.910
Prince Edwin and his friends 
are leveling up well, I think.

00:58.710 --> 01:02.870
The reports told me that William 
charged in as the vanguard,

01:02.870 --> 01:07.000
while His Highness and Oswald 
took out any monsters he missed.

01:07.490 --> 01:11.510
The only problem is that they killed 
all the monsters themselves.

01:11.510 --> 01:15.010
The other students can't 
gain any levels that way.

01:15.440 --> 01:19.000
All they do is lavish the 
three of them with praise.

01:19.000 --> 01:20.270
What about Miss Alicia?

01:21.350 --> 01:25.560
Same as the other students.
She didn't kill a single monster.

01:26.730 --> 01:29.070
Did she seem like she wanted to do more?

01:29.850 --> 01:32.060
The written report doesn't tell me that.

01:32.060 --> 01:34.680
Even if she wanted to do more,

01:34.680 --> 01:37.400
I suppose there was just nothing 
she could do this time.

01:38.070 --> 01:42.330
Those three boys probably wanted to 
show off for the girl they like, too.

01:42.770 --> 01:44.460
<i>Ah...</i>

01:45.090 --> 01:50.580
Since Miss Alicia can use light magic, 
we need her to grow stronger.

01:51.080 --> 01:54.320
I may end up asking for 
your help on that front.

01:54.720 --> 01:58.220
I understand. You can count on me.

01:58.550 --> 02:01.980
<i>When he asks, I'll take her 
to a dark-type dungeon.</i>

02:02.790 --> 02:05.430
<i>Alicia will have an advantage 
against all the monsters there.</i>

02:05.430 --> 02:07.020
<i>She'll be thrilled!</i>

02:10.440 --> 02:12.590
No!

02:14.780 --> 02:16.260
On another subject...

02:16.260 --> 02:19.210
We've received a request from the 
castle's magic tool development team

02:19.210 --> 02:21.920
to test the endurance of some magic tools.

02:21.920 --> 02:22.920
I'll do it.

02:23.980 --> 02:27.620
<i>Magic tools are items that 
have been imbued with magic.</i>

02:28.120 --> 02:30.570
<i>Aside from things like armor and weapons,</i>

02:30.570 --> 02:36.300
<i>they also include my favorite items, the 
Amulet of Growth and Monster-Calling Flute.</i>

02:36.840 --> 02:39.110
This is what they want us to test.

02:39.110 --> 02:40.640
They want to use it to make armor.

02:41.010 --> 02:44.380
It's passed Knight Captain 
Adolf's endurance test,

02:44.840 --> 02:47.770
but they want to know how 
it fares against stronger—

02:47.770 --> 02:48.450
Uh.

02:56.120 --> 02:58.520
Can you describe how much strength that took?

02:58.920 --> 03:01.420
I'll be more careful to take 
note of that next time.

03:03.540 --> 03:06.710
<i>This might be good practice for 
controlling how much strength I use.</i>

03:07.990 --> 03:09.540
I can't even budge it.

03:35.250 --> 03:38.860
<b>Villainess Level 99</b>

03:35.580 --> 03:38.860
I May Be the Hidden Boss but I'm Not the Demon Lord

04:41.280 --> 04:46.530
<b>The Hidden Boss Finds a Conversation Partner</b>

04:52.770 --> 04:53.750
Yumiella!

04:54.980 --> 04:56.150
Master Patrick.

04:56.770 --> 05:00.650
Did the principal want to see you 
about yesterday's field lesson?

05:01.200 --> 05:05.030
Yes. He scolded me for using 
the Monster-Calling Flute.

05:05.360 --> 05:07.310
Well, that's to be expected.

05:07.310 --> 05:08.660
Patrick!

05:09.200 --> 05:11.480
Can you come to the classroom for a minute?

05:11.480 --> 05:15.170
Everyone wants you to take command 
during the next field lesson.

05:15.430 --> 05:16.370
Sure.

05:16.990 --> 05:18.330
Well, see you later.

05:20.580 --> 05:22.790
<i>They really trust him.</i>

05:24.840 --> 05:29.650
<i>My life of solitude has changed a 
bit since the field lesson ended.</i>

05:30.080 --> 05:33.520
<i>Patrick comes by to talk 
to me every now and then.</i>

05:34.010 --> 05:36.640
Now, we're going to do 
some practical exercises.

05:36.640 --> 05:38.530
Everyone, pair up.

05:44.930 --> 05:45.930
Yumiella.

05:47.250 --> 05:49.750
If you don't have anyone to 
pair up with, how about me?

05:50.600 --> 05:51.870
Are you sure?

05:52.300 --> 05:53.240
What do you mean?

05:55.780 --> 05:58.880
You must have plenty of friends 
who want to pair up with you.

05:59.270 --> 06:02.630
Don't worry about them. 
I owe you one, remember?

06:02.890 --> 06:05.190
You mean because I healed you?

06:05.190 --> 06:07.320
Please, don't worry about that.

06:07.320 --> 06:10.890
If I hadn't been there, you could 
have used a potion to heal yourself.

06:11.250 --> 06:14.900
Really? I guess I'll pair 
up with someone else, then.

06:14.900 --> 06:17.590
Uh, actually, please do worry about it.

06:17.590 --> 06:20.280
I'm the one who healed your injury.

06:21.700 --> 06:24.780
You're also the one who caused it, you know.

06:27.360 --> 06:33.540
<i>He might be the closest thing to a friend 
I've found since I reincarnated here.</i>

06:34.230 --> 06:39.550
<i>It must be his natural virtue that made 
everyone else follow his orders, too.</i>

06:39.960 --> 06:44.470
<i>That and, for some reason, his 
voice seems to carry really well.</i>

06:45.130 --> 06:46.150
Let's do this!

06:48.310 --> 06:50.850
<i>Patrick's swordsmanship is beautiful.</i>

06:50.850 --> 06:55.170
<i>Nothing like me and my reliance 
on sheer power and reflexes.</i>

07:01.110 --> 07:02.360
Patrick!

07:05.910 --> 07:07.490
Ow...

07:07.820 --> 07:09.490
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

07:09.740 --> 07:11.240
I'll heal you right now.

07:17.090 --> 07:19.990
Th-Thanks. I'm okay.

07:22.290 --> 07:26.070
I'm sorry. Thank you for pairing up with me.

07:26.070 --> 07:28.340
Nah, I should apologize to you.

07:29.250 --> 07:31.850
Maybe I'm not a worthy partner for you.

07:32.270 --> 07:34.780
No, I don't think that's true.

07:34.780 --> 07:37.600
I could learn a great deal 
from your sword skills.

07:37.880 --> 07:41.620
You want to get even stronger 
by learning how to use a sword?

07:42.150 --> 07:44.110
Just what are you thinking about fighting?

07:44.440 --> 07:48.110
Um... the Demon Lord, I suppose?

07:48.740 --> 07:49.680
The Demon Lord?

07:50.070 --> 07:52.870
So the rumors about him coming 
back in two years are true?

07:53.200 --> 07:55.280
Did you hear something 
about it from the king?

07:55.280 --> 07:56.820
No, nothing.

07:57.200 --> 07:59.630
<i>I lied. Yes, I have heard about it.</i>

07:59.890 --> 08:03.200
Either Prince Edwin was just making things up

08:03.200 --> 08:06.490
or the king is hiding something, I suppose.

08:06.490 --> 08:08.880
I could easily believe either of those.

08:09.130 --> 08:12.280
<i>There have been so many unsavory 
rumors about Prince Edwin lately</i>

08:12.280 --> 08:14.820
<i>that if I said his claims about 
the Demon Lord's return weren't true,</i>

08:14.820 --> 08:17.890
<i>it would be difficult to prove I was lying.</i>

08:18.230 --> 08:21.160
<i>And since he's been flirting 
with Alicia all over the place,</i>

08:21.160 --> 08:22.750
<i>his popularity's dropping.</i>

08:23.270 --> 08:26.050
<i>Many are already saying his 
claims about the Demon Lord</i>

08:26.050 --> 08:28.470
<i>are a nasty joke or just made up.</i>

08:29.540 --> 08:34.430
<i>On the other hand, the rumor that I'm 
the Demon Lord hasn't died out, either.</i>

08:34.430 --> 08:38.150
<i>It may have even been revived after 
what happened during the field lesson.</i>

08:38.870 --> 08:42.420
You don't think I'm the 
Demon Lord, Master Patrick?

08:42.680 --> 08:46.800
If you were the Demon Lord, the world 
would've been wiped out by now.

08:47.350 --> 08:48.300
<i>True.</i>

08:48.950 --> 08:50.870
Of course, I'm just joking,

08:51.250 --> 08:55.310
but it bugs me that your black hair is 
one of the reasons people believe it.

08:57.500 --> 08:58.960
When I was little,

08:59.310 --> 09:02.310
my hair was almost black, 
and it always bothered me.

09:02.930 --> 09:05.980
It started when a relative 
said my hair looked blackish.

09:06.640 --> 09:09.360
My family said I didn't 
need to worry about it,

09:09.690 --> 09:12.320
but I hated my hair after that.

09:13.030 --> 09:15.450
I think it looks whitish, personally.

09:16.340 --> 09:17.590
Whitish?

09:18.520 --> 09:21.240
Compared to yours, yeah, I guess it would.

09:22.600 --> 09:27.760
But that's why I admire the way you 
wear your black hair so confidently.

09:28.540 --> 09:32.530
I promise I'll never look down on you or 
dislike you because of your hair color.

09:34.750 --> 09:37.540
Th-Thank you.

09:38.140 --> 09:42.330
I think your gray hair is quite lovely.

09:42.330 --> 09:43.760
Thanks.

09:43.760 --> 09:46.890
I think your black hair's pretty, too.

09:49.410 --> 09:52.030
Um, shall we have another match?

09:52.440 --> 09:54.660
Sure, I'd love to.

09:55.670 --> 09:56.370
Let's do this!

10:04.280 --> 10:05.500
I'm sorry!

10:05.880 --> 10:07.410
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

10:12.740 --> 10:15.520
I'm fine. It doesn't hurt anymore.

10:16.070 --> 10:19.520
I realized it before, but... your 
healing magic feels pretty nice.

10:19.520 --> 10:21.610
It looks disgusting, though.

10:23.060 --> 10:27.330
You're amazing, Yumiella. You use 
dark magic with such confidence.

10:27.330 --> 10:29.480
I just got lucky.

10:29.480 --> 10:33.280
Magic affinity is just 
something we're born with.

10:33.510 --> 10:35.070
It's not just that.

10:35.070 --> 10:37.680
Even if I could use dark magic,

10:37.990 --> 10:40.780
I'd probably just try to keep it hidden.

10:41.520 --> 10:45.830
Just like with your hair, 
you don't deny who you are.

10:46.260 --> 10:49.720
I think that's something not 
many people can pull off.

10:50.260 --> 10:52.080
Thank you...

10:58.020 --> 11:01.930
<i>Looking back now, I never 
gave much thought to Yumiella</i>

11:02.180 --> 11:04.530
<i>as a character in the game.</i>

11:05.880 --> 11:08.680
Even if I could use dark magic,

11:08.680 --> 11:11.540
I'd probably just try to keep it hidden.

11:12.720 --> 11:18.290
<i>Was the Yumiella in the game 
born with her dark magic, too?</i>

11:18.780 --> 11:26.290
Yumiella

11:18.780 --> 11:26.290
(I've fallen to the darkness...)

11:19.170 --> 11:23.200
<i>The game's explanation was that 
Yumiella obtained her dark magic</i>

11:23.200 --> 11:26.290
<i>because she gave in to the darkness,</i>

11:26.290 --> 11:32.800
Yumiella

11:26.290 --> 11:32.800
(It seemed as though that deep darkness was
calling to me.)

11:26.810 --> 11:29.590
<i>but none of the story scenes 
were clear about it.</i>

11:30.280 --> 11:32.800
<i>Maybe the truth is actually different.</i>

11:32.800 --> 11:41.560
Yumiella

11:32.800 --> 11:41.560
Dark magic? What are you talking about?

11:33.110 --> 11:34.450
<i>It's just a theory,</i>

11:34.450 --> 11:38.340
<i>but what if the game's Yumiella 
could use dark magic all along,</i>

11:38.790 --> 11:41.560
<i>and she just kept it hidden from everyone?</i>

11:41.560 --> 11:48.980
Edwin

11:41.560 --> 11:48.980
Alicia, that light magic you used was amazing!

11:42.130 --> 11:44.360
<i>She must have really hated the heroine,</i>

11:44.720 --> 11:47.330
<i>who used light magic with total confidence</i>

11:47.330 --> 11:48.980
<i>and was loved by everyone.</i>

11:50.940 --> 11:53.230
<i>I guess there's no point 
in thinking about it.</i>

11:53.970 --> 11:58.230
<i>This world is just this 
world. It's not the game.</i>

12:01.650 --> 12:02.910
<i>A few days later,</i>

12:03.250 --> 12:05.750
<i>we had our second field lesson.</i>

12:10.130 --> 12:11.930
I'm sure you know this by now,

12:11.930 --> 12:14.760
but don't you dare use your 
Monster-Calling Flute again.

12:15.000 --> 12:19.350
I won't. The principal 
yelled at me about it, too.

12:19.350 --> 12:23.010
And no burning down the forest 
just because you're bored, either.

12:23.480 --> 12:24.770
I know.

12:24.770 --> 12:28.230
Today, I'm the battlefield medic.

12:28.870 --> 12:31.000
It's a lesson, not a war...

12:36.170 --> 12:39.440
The monsters you face today are of 
a different type than the last ones.

12:39.440 --> 12:41.740
Be careful not to let your 
guard down at any time.

12:44.810 --> 12:45.920
So bored...

12:46.320 --> 12:47.410
Dark Bind.

12:49.920 --> 12:51.840
Rock, paper, scissors.

12:51.840 --> 12:53.740
Rock, paper, scissors.

12:55.340 --> 12:57.840
<i>I'm a supervisor... a supervisor...</i>

13:00.760 --> 13:03.800
<i>It looks like they're steadily 
getting good results,</i>

13:04.110 --> 13:06.560
<i>but the atmosphere feels much 
more lax than last time.</i>

13:07.360 --> 13:09.570
<i>Times like these are when 
the danger is greatest.</i>

13:11.610 --> 13:13.690
Yes, I'm coming to heal you.

13:13.950 --> 13:16.810
You don't need to do that, Miss Yumiella...

13:16.810 --> 13:19.030
Well, I had nothing else to do.

13:19.830 --> 13:22.650
Would you like a potion or healing magic?

13:22.650 --> 13:23.880
Potion, please!

13:25.120 --> 13:29.790
But if I heal you with magic, there's 
no need to waste potions, is there?

13:30.160 --> 13:32.000
Why even ask us, then?

13:32.580 --> 13:33.800
I'll heal you.

13:39.280 --> 13:42.510
Everything's fine. You're as good as new.

13:45.470 --> 13:49.820
<i>Funny... Healers are 
usually pretty popular...</i>

13:50.820 --> 13:53.770
Okay, we're going to take a break for a bit.

13:55.150 --> 13:58.480
<i>This lax attitude they all 
have is definitely a problem.</i>

13:58.480 --> 14:00.780
<i>When you're trying to raise your level,</i>

14:01.060 --> 14:03.300
<i>you need to be right on 
the brink at all times.</i>

14:04.780 --> 14:06.270
<i>Which means...</i>

14:07.640 --> 14:09.750
I told you not to use this.

14:09.750 --> 14:13.060
You shouldn't have even brought 
it. It's too dangerous.

14:13.060 --> 14:15.130
The current scenario is more dangerous.

14:15.130 --> 14:18.040
Isn't it important to feel 
some degree of urgency?

14:18.280 --> 14:22.050
And I believe all of these students 
are skilled enough to handle it.

14:22.890 --> 14:26.430
The difficulty of the lesson should be 
raised in proportion to their levels.

14:26.430 --> 14:28.290
You have a point, but...

14:28.670 --> 14:31.640
We could even send each one of 
them into their own dungeon.

14:31.640 --> 14:33.520
That's the one thing we can't do!

14:34.240 --> 14:36.620
You'd have to be crazy to 
go into a dungeon alone!

14:37.590 --> 14:39.940
Are you denying my entire past?

14:39.940 --> 14:42.190
Uh, no, I didn't mean to...

14:42.190 --> 14:45.300
The method we're using now 
is too inefficient, anyway.

14:45.300 --> 14:49.280
Making people kill low-level 
monsters in groups is wasteful.

14:50.020 --> 14:53.540
Couldn't they face monsters 
of a slightly higher level?

14:53.750 --> 14:57.730
Even you said the lesson was 
too inefficient last time.

14:57.730 --> 14:59.040
Yeah, but...

14:59.500 --> 15:01.370
Even if I don't use the flute,

15:01.370 --> 15:05.650
I'd be fine with it if everyone
would just take this more seriously.

15:06.150 --> 15:06.800
I know!

15:07.430 --> 15:09.100
A different method would be fine, right?

15:09.850 --> 15:14.310
What if I injured everyone with 
my magic and then healed them?

15:14.930 --> 15:19.110
Knowing how much an injury hurts 
should tighten their focus more.

15:20.390 --> 15:24.340
Oh, don't worry. I'm pretty sure I 
can hurt them without killing them.

15:24.340 --> 15:26.070
Do you hear yourself?!

15:26.720 --> 15:29.070
The flute or an injury? Choose one.

15:29.390 --> 15:30.580
Flute, please...

15:30.840 --> 15:33.580
That settles it. It's okay, right, Patrick?

15:40.230 --> 15:42.960
Assume formation! Prepare to engage!

15:43.670 --> 15:47.140
<i>Oh, shoot. I forgot to be polite.</i>

15:47.140 --> 15:48.830
<i>And I just called him "Patrick"...</i>

15:51.430 --> 15:54.100
Don't break formation! Stay calm!

15:54.590 --> 15:58.870
<i>I always get a little overzealous 
when it comes to leveling up.</i>

15:58.870 --> 16:00.360
<i>I'm a count's daughter,</i>

16:00.930 --> 16:03.090
<i>and Patrick is a margrave's son.</i>

16:03.090 --> 16:05.360
<i>He ranks higher than me, and I...</i>

16:06.160 --> 16:09.250
<i>If I draw the ire of the Ashbatten family,</i>

16:09.250 --> 16:12.980
<i>the entire Dolkness family's 
reputation as nobility will drop.</i>

16:13.870 --> 16:17.600
<i>I guess that's no problem.
My family's problematic as it is.</i>

16:18.130 --> 16:18.620
<i>But...</i>

16:19.460 --> 16:25.200
<i>The idea of Patrick hating me... 
might make me a little sad...</i>

16:26.550 --> 16:27.900
Maintain formation!

16:28.550 --> 16:31.760
Just do this the way you've 
practiced, and you can win!

16:32.340 --> 16:36.270
<i>Is he using wind magic 
to make his voice carry?</i>

16:36.530 --> 16:39.390
Now! Rear guard, attack with magic!

16:42.290 --> 16:46.130
<i>So it's magic that makes his 
voice resonate like that.</i>

16:47.720 --> 16:51.070
<i>And he's using earth magic to keep 
his feet planted at the same time.</i>

16:51.700 --> 16:54.330
<i>That's something I could never do myself.</i>

16:54.760 --> 16:57.830
<i>Patrick might be a genius when 
it comes to group combat.</i>

16:58.710 --> 17:02.660
<i>How should I interact with him after this?</i>

17:06.500 --> 17:08.090
Looks like things have calmed down.

17:08.930 --> 17:10.220
Good work.

17:10.540 --> 17:13.000
Patrick! Thanks so much!

17:12.230 --> 17:14.430
You were so dashing, Master Ashbatten!

17:13.610 --> 17:15.470
You saved us again!

17:24.860 --> 17:30.000
<i>I returned to the academy without exchanging 
any further words with Patrick.</i>

17:30.390 --> 17:35.580
<i>Even if he does end up hating 
me and stops talking to me,</i>

17:35.890 --> 17:39.090
<i>if I just think of it as going back to 
how things where when school started,</i>

17:39.090 --> 17:41.330
<i>it's nothing I need to 
stress over too much...</i>

17:42.020 --> 17:43.340
<i>Or it shouldn't be...</i>

17:43.340 --> 17:44.570
Miss Yumiella!

17:47.840 --> 17:50.720
Yes? What is it, Miss Alicia?

17:50.990 --> 17:51.930
Um...

17:53.850 --> 17:58.470
I'm sorry for just assuming you 
were the Demon Lord the other day.

17:59.940 --> 18:03.980
I know I caused trouble for you 
by carelessly blurting that out.

18:04.610 --> 18:08.680
<i>Just standing in front of me 
now must be terrifying for her.</i>

18:08.680 --> 18:10.740
<i>Yet she still came to apologize...</i>

18:11.320 --> 18:13.360
<i>She really is a nice girl.</i>

18:14.900 --> 18:16.740
Stay away from Alicia!

18:17.670 --> 18:21.000
I heard what you did during the field lesson.

18:21.470 --> 18:23.410
You used a Monster-Calling Flute

18:23.410 --> 18:26.570
to force the students to fight 
a whole horde of monsters.

18:27.030 --> 18:30.480
Were you trying to kill someone 
and make it look like an accident?

18:30.480 --> 18:31.760
H-Huh?!

18:32.070 --> 18:35.010
<i>Sounds like he heard an exaggerated 
version of the story.</i>

18:35.310 --> 18:40.280
Or was it a plot to injure students
and then heal them, as if it were a favor,

18:40.280 --> 18:42.640
to make yourself more popular?

18:43.460 --> 18:46.210
You might not be the Demon Lord,

18:46.210 --> 18:50.400
but you're still a danger 
to the Kingdom of Valschein.

18:50.400 --> 18:55.630
Don't forget that I'll have my eye on 
you as long as you're at this academy.

18:50.400 --> 18:57.010
<i>I suppose I really am a maverick in 
this academy... no, in this world.</i>

18:55.960 --> 18:57.550
If you endanger the students again...

18:57.550 --> 19:00.410
<i>Is it even necessary to go 
through all this to stay here?</i>

19:00.920 --> 19:02.550
<i>I don't even have any friends.</i>

19:03.670 --> 19:06.920
<i>But even if I run away from this academy,</i>

19:07.260 --> 19:11.870
<i>is there a place for me 
anywhere else in this world?</i>

19:12.730 --> 19:14.800
Please wait a moment, Your Highness!

19:17.500 --> 19:19.300
Patrick Ashbatten?

19:20.150 --> 19:23.530
It's true that Yumiella used 
a Monster-Calling Flute.

19:23.530 --> 19:27.310
But she did it to make the students 
take the lesson seriously.

19:27.890 --> 19:32.280
She wasn't in the wrong... 
Well, maybe she was, but...

19:32.640 --> 19:33.530
<i>Truth.</i>

19:33.530 --> 19:38.990
But her methods are relatively 
popular among the regional nobles!

19:40.020 --> 19:43.970
Her method truly is the most 
efficient for leveling up.

19:43.970 --> 19:46.750
And she didn't violate any 
school rules or kingdom laws.

19:47.390 --> 19:50.750
I would like you to stay out of this matter.

19:58.240 --> 20:00.400
I'll back down for now.

20:00.400 --> 20:02.020
Let's go, Alicia.

20:10.880 --> 20:13.460
<i>Something tells me he's furious.</i>

20:15.370 --> 20:17.530
That must've been really rough for you.

20:17.530 --> 20:20.730
Huh? Uh... Th-Thank you...

20:20.730 --> 20:24.410
Um, are you sure it was wise 
to say that to the prince?

20:24.410 --> 20:27.430
Well, I'm still the son of a margrave.

20:27.430 --> 20:30.670
Being detested by the second 
prince is nothing to me.

20:31.380 --> 20:34.670
Also... are you angry?

20:34.980 --> 20:37.940
I'm not so much angry as exasperated.

20:37.940 --> 20:41.180
Maybe he just lacks awareness 
of his own royal standing.

20:41.660 --> 20:44.180
<i>Uh, I wasn't talking about Edwin.</i>

20:44.180 --> 20:46.660
Um... I'm sorry.

20:46.660 --> 20:50.940
I know I got a bit excited, but I spoke 
too casually to you during the lesson.

20:51.220 --> 20:54.150
Huh? That's what you were worried about?

20:54.150 --> 20:56.870
It's not like I'm some 
big-headed central noble.

20:56.870 --> 21:00.450
It doesn't bother me. Talk to me 
however you feel the most comfortable.

21:00.740 --> 21:02.380
<i>That's it?</i>

21:02.380 --> 21:06.190
<i>But the hierarchy is supposed to 
be very important in noble society.</i>

21:06.190 --> 21:09.460
<i>Is it really all right to 
just wrap it up like that?</i>

21:09.960 --> 21:12.390
I don't care much for formalities.

21:12.390 --> 21:16.340
There are way too many other things 
you should be more worried about.

21:16.890 --> 21:18.340
<i>I do agree there.</i>

21:18.800 --> 21:21.910
Oh, right. Did you want 
to see me for something?

21:21.910 --> 21:27.250
Yeah. You seemed a bit down after 
the field lesson, so I was worried.

21:27.250 --> 21:28.730
Did something happen?

21:29.410 --> 21:32.170
I was just having a little 
bit of depression time.

21:32.170 --> 21:33.730
I'm fine now.

21:33.940 --> 21:36.480
Okay, then. Glad to hear it.

21:37.010 --> 21:38.360
Ready to go back to class?

21:39.610 --> 21:40.900
Master Patrick...

21:41.470 --> 21:42.740
Just "Patrick" is fine.

21:43.190 --> 21:44.330
Patrick...

21:46.040 --> 21:47.050
Thanks.

21:50.020 --> 21:52.980
It's unusual to see you smile like that.

21:53.470 --> 21:55.250
Was I smiling?

21:57.540 --> 21:58.250
Let's go.

21:58.510 --> 21:59.220
Sure.

21:59.970 --> 22:03.510
<i>I think I'd like to be 
friends with him, if I can.</i>

22:04.150 --> 22:07.930
<i>But I'm sure that'd be asking too much.</i>
